<title>USA: Atlas in offer for Prime Service debt.</title>
<headline>Atlas in offer for Prime Service debt.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlas Copco AB's North America unit said on Thursday it began an offer for $66.7 million in the outstanding debt of Prime Service Inc, which Atlas Copco recently acquired.</p>
<p>Sweden-based Atlas said in a news release made available in the United States that Atlas Copco North America Inc's offer is for all outstanding Prime Service 12.75 percent notes due 2005.</p>
<p>The total consideration to be paid will be based on a fixed spread of 50 basis points over the yield to maturity on the 5-7/8 percent U.S. Treasury Notes due Feb. 15, 2000.</p>
<p>The purchase price will be set on August 4. The offer will expire August 6.</p>
</text>
